{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggbz8fQf6SHfqSjCpU3Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fitted the three bands to the d⁵ ligand-field energy matrices on the low-spin side, holding C/B at 4.6. The result is **Dq ≈ 2715 cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 27 150 cm⁻¹), B ≈ 877 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 4035 cm⁻¹**.\n\n**Approach**\n- The ground term is ²T₂g (t₂g⁵), so the only spin-allowed d–d bands are doublet → doublet transitions.\n- The fitting tool takes C as a fixed number, not as a ratio to B. So I fitted Dq and B for a set C, then reset C to 4.6 × B and fitted again.\n  - First pass, with the tool's default C = 3850: Dq = 2704 and B = 878. That gives C/B = 4.38, which is not the required ratio.\n  - Second pass, with C = 4040 (about 4.6 × 878): Dq = 2716, B = 876.6 and C/B = 4.61. Each band is reproduced to within 1 cm⁻¹.\n- One more step would change B by less than 1 cm⁻¹ and Dq by only a few cm⁻¹, so I stopped there.\n\n**Band assignments from the final fit (ground term ²T₂g)**\n\n| Observed (cm⁻¹) | Calculated (cm⁻¹) | Assignment |\n|---|---|---|\n| 22 640 | 22 639 | ²T₂g → ²A₂g |\n| 22 930 | 22 931 | ²T₂g → ²T₁g |\n| 25 080 | 25 080 | ²T₂g → ²T₂g(b) |\n\nThe next doublet band is predicted at about 27 200 cm⁻¹ (²E_g).\n\n**Low-spin check:** With these parameters the high-spin state (⁶A₁g) lies about 3500 cm⁻¹ above the ²T₂g ground state. So the low-spin assignment holds.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2715, \"B\": 877, \"C\": 4035, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Low-spin d5 doublet bands fitted with C/B=4.6 reproduce all three peaks within 1 cm-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2734,"cache_read_input_tokens":10801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2734,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics"